 would not  have been possible without the european  the the european astronaut corp european  space agency and the roles of all the  countries involved with space  uh i would like to say even more i am  even more than european i believe that  that the future should be of a global  understanding that we are all humans  traveling in one spacecraft we call it  planet earth but we are traveling to  space in the one planet that we know  supports life so we need to be together  understanding that this is our only home  and that we need to  treat it really well and be  understanding uh in order to continue in  our future the experience of being in  orbit for six months is so unique in a  way and  the environment is so unique that my  idea was that if there was something i  could do on the ground then i wouldn't  do it while i was up there and it was a  conscious effort not to not to miss it  instead i tried to do things that were  not possible anywhere else the space  station is very big it's a it's an  amazing environment and i didn't miss  any of the small things  you can really do without the small  things when you have so much more when  you are in orbit every time i tell my  story every time i relieve my story it's  almost as if i'm doing it all over again  and i'm and also i i'm letting people  take part in it being an active  participant in my experience so when i  was in orbit i i was communicating to  the ground through blogs through the  social network social media and out of  that experience came the book bolade  that i wrote bolare means flying and  it's also a very famous italian song but  it's something everybody can identify  with both in italy and outside of italy  so the book is a collection of the  stories that i that i brought while i  was in space so  really it's it's the first book that was  written in space one more thing that is  very important for me it's also a way to  give back all my proceedings will go  into a scholarship to let other people  e